==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm|en}}, from {{etyl|fro|en}} {{term|tribut|lang=fro}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|tributum||tribute, literally 'a thing contributed or paid'|lang=la}}, neuter of {{term|tributus}}, past participle of {{term|tribuere||to assign, allot, grant, give, bestow, etc.}}, usually derived, from {{term|tribus||tribe}}; see [[tribe]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en-us-tribute.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# An [[acknowledgment]] of [[gratitude]], [[respect]] or [[admiration]]; an [[accompanying]] [[gift]].
#: ''Please accept this as a '''tribute''' of our thanks.''
#* Gray
#*: the passing '''tribute''' of a sigh
# A [[payment]] made by one [[nation]] to another in [[submission]].
#: ''The Ancient Romans made their conquered countries pay '''tribute'''.''
# [[extortion|Extortion]]; [[protection]] [[money]].
# A payment made by a [[feudal]] [[vassal]] to his [[lord]].
# {{context|mining|lang=en}} A certain proportion of the mined [[ore]], or of its [[value]], given to the [[miner]] as [[payment]].
#: {{rfquotek|Pryce}}
#: {{rfquotek|Tomlinson}}

